{"text": "The Smell of Rain.\n\nWater fell on Nia's hair, her face and her arms.\n\nShe laughed and turned around and around.\n\n\"Rain!\" she shouted. \"It's raining!\"\n\nIt was warmer than she expected. It was softer, too.\n\nThen Leo walked out of the dark. He was wet, and his shoes were very dirty.\n\n\"Is this it?\" asked Nia. \"Is this real rain?\"\n\n\"Yes,\" said Leo. But he didn't look at her.\n\nNia closed her eyes. She breathed in slowly and deeply.\n\nShe waited for the smell. The sweet smell of the earth from his letter.\n\nBut there was nothing. The air smelled of water and a little of metal. It smelled the same as the water in Lunaria.\n\nNia opened her eyes and looked up.\n\nAbove the house, she saw stars. Lots of stars, and only one small cloud. And the water did not come from above. It came from the side, from somewhere near her window.\n\nThen the water stopped.\n\nEverything was quiet. Leo didn't move.\n\nThey sat on the wet steps for almost an hour.\n\nFar away, there was a low sound, like a big drum.\n\nThe wind changed. It was colder now, much colder. The small cloud was not alone anymore. A dark wall of clouds came over the hill.\n\nThe first drop hit Nia on the nose. It was cold! Then another, and another. Then the whole sky opened.\n\nThis water was different. It was heavier and colder, and it came from high above.\n\nThen the smell came. It came up from the dry ground, sweet and deep. It smelled like bread, old wood and something new.\n\nNobody needed to tell Nia. She knew.\n\n\"This is rain,\" she said softly. \"This is the real rain.\"\n\nLeo stood next to her. He turned his face up to the sky too.\n\n\"I'm sorry,\" he said. \"The first rain was me. I turned on the pipes. The one under your window.\"\n\n\"I know,\" said Nia. \"Your rain was warmer. And it had no smell.\"\n\n\"You were so sad. I only wanted…\"\n\n\"I know,\" she said again, and she smiled. \"It was the kindest rain in the world.\"\n\nThey laughed and stayed outside until they were very, very wet. Grandma Edda came out with an umbrella. Then she closed it and stood with them.\n\nThat night, Nia wrote in her notebook. Rain is colder than you think. It is heavier, too. And it smells better than anything on the Moon.", "textSha256": "0dc9dfd3b0af06bc528616aeca439bb6b1250770a6288393eb8ef75ff25f0383", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "S", "m", "e", "l", "l", " ", "o", "f", " ", "R", "a", "i", "n", ".", "\n", "\n", "W", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "f", "e", "l", "l", " ", "o", "n", " ", "N", "i", "a", "'", "s", " ", "h", "a", "i", "r", ",", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "f", "a", "c", "e", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "a", "r", "m", "s", ".", "\n", "\n", "S", "h", "e", " ", "l", "a", "u", "g", "h", "e", "d", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "u", "r", "n", "e", "d", " ", "a", "r", "o", "u", "n", "d", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "a", "r", "o", "u", "n", "d", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "R", "a", "i", "n", "!", "\"", " ", "s", "h", "e", " ", "s", "h", "o", "u", "t", "e", "d", ".", " ", "\"", "I", "t", "'", "s", " ", "r", "a", "i", "n", "i", "n", "g", "!", "\"", "\n", "\n", "I", "t", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "w", "a", "r", "m", "e", "r", " ", "t", "h", "a", "n", " ", "s", "h", "e", " ", "e", "x", "p", "e", "c", "t", "e", "d", ".", " ", "I", "t", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "s", "o", "f", "t", "e", "r", ",", " ", "t", "o", "o", ".", "\n", "\n", "T", "h", "e", "n", " ", "L", "e", "o", " ", "w", "a", "l", "k", "e", "d", " ", "o", "u", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "d", "a", "r", "k", ".", " ", "H", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "w", "e", "t", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "h", "i", "s", " ", "s", "h", "o", "e", "s", " ", "w", "e", "r", "e", " ", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "d", "i", "r", "t", "y", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "I", "s", " ", "t", "h", "i", "s", " ", "i", "t", "?", "\"", " ", "a", "s", "k", "e", "d", " ", "N", "i",